 Cloudflare Worker API for OpenReel template storage and sharing.
 
+## Authentication and deployment status
+
+This backend is not ready for public production deployment. It has no production
+identity verifier. All non-GET/HEAD/OPTIONS requests now fail with HTTP 401 unless
+trusted server authentication middleware establishes a `verifiedIdentity` context
+principal. Caller-supplied bearer/user/creator headers are never an identity, and
+setting `ENVIRONMENT=development` or `test` does not enable a bypass. Existing API
+tests inject a principal through a test-only wrapper, outside deployed code.
+
+This deliberately disables unauthenticated template mutations, share uploads,
+AI/highlight jobs, marketplace events and crash uploads. Public discovery reads
+remain available. Before enabling authenticated operations, implement and test a
+real credential verifier, creator/reviewer authorization, ownership checks,
+durable rate limits, body limits and a privacy/abuse review. These changes are a
+fail-closed safety boundary, not a complete authentication implementation. The
+deployment examples below describe infrastructure setup, not production approval.
+
 ## Features
 
 - **Template Storage**: Upload and store templates in Cloudflare R2
